  <!-- SECTION 4: CHANGE HISTORY -->
  <section id="assembly-history" aria-labelledby="assembly-history-heading">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="assembly-history-heading">Assembly Change History</h2></div>
      <p>Chronological development and key improvements across maize reference genome releases.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-panel">
    <div class="assembly-history-timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-badge">v5</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0 \(2020\)</h3>
          <p>De novo long-read assembly using PacBio Sequel technology coupled with high-coverage BioNano optical genome maps. Captures complex repetitive regions, centromeric arrays, and structural variants with contig N50 increased to 25.6 Mb. Accompanied by pan-genome assemblies for 26 NAM founder lines.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-badge">v4</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0 \(2017\)</h3>
          <p>Complete de novo assembly using PacBio RS II single-molecule sequencing on tissue derived from PI 677128. Resolved thousands of misassemblies, orientation errors, and gap regions from Sanger BAC physical maps, boosting contig N50 from 40 kb to 1.18 Mb \(Jiao et al. 2017\).</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-badge">v3</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>B73 RefGen_v3 \(2013\)</h3>
          <p>Captured missing gene space in v2 using whole-genome shotgun \(WGS\) sequence reads. Integrated 213 new gene models, refined 251 models, and resolved contig order/orientation across chromosomes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-badge">v2</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>B73 RefGen_v2 \(2010\)</h3>
          <p>Iterative improvement on the initial BAC physical map by correcting contig order and orientation within BACs using the minimum tiling path \(MTP\). Upgraded gene model set from 4a to 5b.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-badge">v1</div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>B73 RefGen_v1 \(2009\)</h3>
          <p>Initial publication of the complete maize B73 reference genome using BAC-by-BAC Sanger sequencing anchored by fingerprint contig \(FPC\) physical and genetic maps \(Schnable et al. 2009, Wei et al. 2009\).</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  
    </div>
  </section>

