  <!-- SECTION 8: KEY PUBLICATIONS -->
  <section id="assembly-publications" aria-labelledby="assembly-pubs-heading">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="assembly-pubs-heading">Key Reference Genome Publications</h2></div>
      <p>Primary landmark peer-reviewed research papers establishing the maize reference genome assemblies, annotations, and pan-genome foundations.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-panel">
    <div class="assembly-pubs-list">
      <!-- 1: Hufford et al. 2021 -->
      <article class="reference-result-card">
        <div class="reference-result-meta">
          <span>2021</span><span>Research Article</span><span>Science</span><span>DOI</span><span>PubMed</span>
        </div>
        <h3><a href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5289" target="_blank" rel="noopener">De novo assembly, annotation, and comparative analysis of 26 diverse maize genomes</a></h3>
        <p class="reference-result-authors">Hufford MB, Seetharam AS, Woodhouse MR, Chougule KM, Ou S, Liu J, Ricci WA, Guo T, Olson A, Qing Y, et al.</p>
        <p class="reference-result-citation">Science &bull; 373\(6555\) &bull; 655-662 &bull; doi:10.1126/science.abg5289</p>
        <p class="reference-result-abstract">Maize is a cornerstone crop with exceptional genetic diversity. Here we report high-quality de novo chromosome-level genome assemblies and comprehensive annotations for 26 inbred lines representing the Nested Association Mapping \(NAM\) founder population, alongside an improved B73 reference genome \(NAM-5.0\). Comparative pan-genomic analyses reveal vast structural variation, transposable element dynamics, and variable gene content across modern temperate, tropical, and sweet corn lineages.</p>
        <div class="reference-result-links">
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5289" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="10.1126/science.abg5289">Copy DOI</button>
          <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34353948/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="34353948">Copy PMID</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 2: Jiao et al. 2017 -->
      <article class="reference-result-card">
        <div class="reference-result-meta">
          <span>2017</span><span>Research Article</span><span>Nature</span><span>DOI</span><span>PubMed</span>
        </div>
        <h3><a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/nature22971" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Improved maize reference genome with single-molecule technologies</a></h3>
        <p class="reference-result-authors">Jiao Y, Peluso P, Shi J, Liang T, Stitzer MC, Wang B, Campbell MS, Stein JC, Wei X, Chin CS, et al.</p>
        <p class="reference-result-citation">Nature &bull; 546\(7659\) &bull; 524-527 &bull; doi:10.1038/nature22971</p>
        <p class="reference-result-abstract">Maize is an important genetic model and major crop. However, its complex genome with over 85% repetitive transposable elements challenged short-read assembly. Here we present a reference assembly of B73 \(RefGen_v4\) using single-molecule real-time sequencing and optical mapping. This assembly increases contiguity by 52-fold, closes over 100,000 gaps, corrects structural misassemblies, and refines the Filtered Gene Set.</p>
        <div class="reference-result-links">
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1038/nature22971" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="10.1038/nature22971">Copy DOI</button>
          <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28605751/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="28605751">Copy PMID</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 3: Law et al. 2015 -->
      <article class="reference-result-card">
        <div class="reference-result-meta">
          <span>2015</span><span>Research Article</span><span>Plant Physiology</span><span>DOI</span><span>PubMed</span>
        </div>
        <h3><a href="https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.114.245027" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Automated update, revision, and quality control of the maize genome annotations using MAKER-P improves the B73 RefGen_v3 gene models and identifies new genes</a></h3>
        <p class="reference-result-authors">Law M, Childs KL, Campbell MS, Stein JC, Soto-Del Valle XM, Wei S, Liang C, Lu Z, Andorf CM, Ware D, Yandell M.</p>
        <p class="reference-result-citation">Plant Physiol. &bull; 167\(1\) &bull; 25-39 &bull; doi:10.1104/pp.114.245027</p>
        <p class="reference-result-abstract">Accurate structural annotation of plant genomes is vital for functional characterization. Using the MAKER-P pipeline, we updated the B73 RefGen_v3 genome annotation, improving existing gene models, identifying missing loci, and providing comprehensive quality-control metrics across protein-coding transcripts.</p>
        <div class="reference-result-links">
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1104/pp.114.245027" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="10.1104/pp.114.245027">Copy DOI</button>
          <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25398939/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="25398939">Copy PMID</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 4: Schnable et al. 2009 -->
      <article class="reference-result-card">
        <div class="reference-result-meta">
          <span>2009</span><span>Landmark Paper</span><span>Science</span><span>DOI</span><span>PubMed</span>
        </div>
        <h3><a href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1178534" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The B73 maize genome: complexity, diversity, and dynamics</a></h3>
        <p class="reference-result-authors">Schnable PS, Ware D, Fulton RS, Stein JC, Wei F, Pasternak S, Liang C, Zhang J, Fulton L, Graves TA, et al.</p>
        <p class="reference-result-citation">Science &bull; 326\(5956\) &bull; 1112-1115 &bull; doi:10.1126/science.1178534</p>
        <p class="reference-result-abstract">We report a 2.3-gigabase reference sequence of the maize inbred line B73. The genome exhibits paleopolyploid ancestry, extensive retrotransposon expansions comprising ~85% of nuclear DNA, and substantial structural divergence that fuels hybrid vigor and phenotypic variation.</p>
        <div class="reference-result-links">
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1178534" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="10.1126/science.1178534">Copy DOI</button>
          <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19965430/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="19965430">Copy PMID</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 5: Wei et al. 2009 -->
      <article class="reference-result-card">
        <div class="reference-result-meta">
          <span>2009</span><span>Research Article</span><span>PLoS Genetics</span><span>DOI</span><span>PubMed</span>
        </div>
        <h3><a href="https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1000715" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The physical and genetic framework of the maize B73 genome</a></h3>
        <p class="reference-result-authors">Wei F, Zhang J, Zhou S, He R, Schaeffer M, Kollner TG, Tao Q, Dong J, Gardiner J, Coe E, et al.</p>
        <p class="reference-result-citation">PLoS Genet. &bull; 5\(11\) &bull; e1000715 &bull; doi:10.1371/journal.pgen.1000715</p>
        <p class="reference-result-abstract">High-resolution physical maps integrated with genetic markers are foundational for assembling large repeat-rich eukaryotic genomes. Here we describe the construction of the agarose and polyacrylamide fingerprint contig physical map of B73 anchored by over 10,000 markers.</p>
        <div class="reference-result-links">
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1000715" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="10.1371/journal.pgen.1000715">Copy DOI</button>
          <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19936064/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="19936064">Copy PMID</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 6: Wei et al. 2007 -->
      <article class="reference-result-card">
        <div class="reference-result-meta">
          <span>2007</span><span>Research Article</span><span>PLoS Genetics</span><span>DOI</span><span>PubMed</span>
        </div>
        <h3><a href="https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.0030123" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Physical and genetic structure of the maize genome reflects its complex evolutionary history</a></h3>
        <p class="reference-result-authors">Wei F, Coe E, Nelson W, Bharti AK, Engler F, Butler E, Kim H, Goicoechea JL, Chen M, Lee S, et al.</p>
        <p class="reference-result-citation">PLoS Genet. &bull; 3\(7\) &bull; e123 &bull; doi:10.1371/journal.pgen.0030123</p>
        <p class="reference-result-abstract">Characterization of the maize genome architecture provides fundamental insights into genome evolution following allotetraploidization, including extensive gene fractionation and structural rearrangements across homeologous chromosomes.</p>
        <div class="reference-result-links">
          <a href="https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.0030123" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="10.1371/journal.pgen.0030123">Copy DOI</button>
          <a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17658955/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PubMed &#8599;</a>
          <button class="reference-copy-id" type="button" data-copy-value="17658955">Copy PMID</button>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- 7: Bi et al. 2006 -->
      <article class="reference-result-card">
        <div class="reference-result-meta">
          <span>2006</span><span>Research Article</span><span>Crop Science</span><span>DOI</span>
        </div>
        <h3><a href="https://doi.org/10.2135/cropsci2004.0706" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Single nucleotide polymorphisms and insertion&ndash;deletions for genetic markers and anchoring the maize fingerprint contig physical map</a></h3>
        <p class="reference-result-authors">Bi I, McMullen MD, Sanchez-Villeda H, Schroeder SG, Fang Z, McMullen M, Polacco M, McMullen M, Coe E.</p>
        <p class="reference-result-citation">Crop Sci. &bull; 46\(1\) &bull; 12-21 &bull; doi:10.2135/cropsci2004.0706</p>
        <p class="reference-result-abstract">Development of high-throughput SNP and indel markers anchored to the B73 fingerprint contig map to connect genetic linkage maps with physical clones across the ten maize chromosomes.</p>
        <div class="reference-result-links">
